      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:00:03 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>After Brent crude’s 10-day decline of nearly 25%, it’s tempting to say the market is pricing in peace. It isn’t. Rather than anticipating that hostilities between the US and Iran are over, traders are foreseeing no immediate risk of a third round of fighting. If the two countries reach a deal, however fragile, oil will trade significantly cheaper than its current value of around $90 a barrel.</description>
